 other special character. The space ( ) is one of the more important nonprinting characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1998713">non-printable character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634937">නිර්මුද්‍රණ අනුලකුණ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11241_85464_634937"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character used to control the format of displayed or printed information, rather than to represent a particular letter, digit, or other special character. The space ( ) is one of the more important nonprinting characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85464">nonprinting character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634937">නිර්මුද්‍රණ අනුලකුණ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11245_59333_1370282"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A sequence of shades ranging from black through white, used in computer graphics to add detail to images or to represent a color image on a monochrome output device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="59333">grayscale</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1370282">අළුවන් පරාසය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11246_24169_635137"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To scan a database, a list of files, or the Internet, either for a particular item or for anything that seems to be of interest.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="24169">browse</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635137">පිරික්සන්න</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11246_385260_635137"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To scan a database, a list of files, or the Internet, either for a particular item or for anything that seems to be of interest.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="385260">browse for</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635137">පිරික්සන්න</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11249_1166159_634315"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Light that is beyond red in the color spectrum. While the light is not visible to the human eye, infrared transmitters and receivers can send and receive infrared signals.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1166159">infrared light</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634315">අධෝරක්ත</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11249_66343_634315"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Light that is beyond red in the color spectrum. While the light is not visible to the human eye, infrared transmitters and receivers can send and receive infrared signals.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="66343">infrared</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634315">අධෝරක්ත</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11249_66344_634315"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Light that is beyond red in the color spectrum. While the light is not visible to the human eye, infrared transmitters and receivers can send and receive infrared signals.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="66344">IR</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634315">අධෝරක්ත</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11251_209886_635493"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Someone who visits a Web site and purposefully supplies personal information, such as name, address, and phone number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="209886">registered user</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635493">ලියාපදිංචි පරිශීලක</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11257_211083_1462085"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables records managers to create and manage entries to a “Holds list” such that any document, image, or webpage on that list cannot be deleted, modified, or allowed to expire until the item is removed from the list. The feature is typically used for items that are subject to events such as litigation, audits, or investigations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="211083">Hold</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1462085">රඳවනය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11264_233734_1913267"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of files that can be delivered as a unit to a client computer or device for installation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="233734">deployment package</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913267">විහිදුම් පැකේජය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11268_2461481_1816537"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Control Panel feature that is used to set restrictions on what traffic is allowed to enter your network from the Internet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2461481">Windows Defender Firewall</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1816537">Windows ෆයර්වෝල්</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11268_2461481_2466706"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Control Panel feature that is used to set restrictions on what traffic is allowed to enter your network from the Internet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2461481">Windows Defender Firewall</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2466706">Windows ආරක්‍ෂකයා ෆයර්වෝල්</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">No