teraction with the databases on machines that do not have a database application installed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1162703">Access Services</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1462159">Access සේවා</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24825_1176677_1462159"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A scalable Web platform that enables users to publish an Access database application to a SharePoint site. Data in these databases can then be viewed and edited in a Web browser. This enables browser-based viewing and interaction with the databases on machines that do not have a database application installed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1176677">Microsoft Access Services</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1462159">Access සේවා</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24826_1162704_1954367"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A server technology enabling users to load, calculate, and display Excel workbooks on Microsoft Office SharePoint Server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1162704">Excel Services</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1954367">Excel Services</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24856_1162836_2290373"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A removable storage device that has been configured with Office applications using the Office To-Go Device Manager.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1162836">Office enabled device</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2290373">office සක්‍රීය උපාංගය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2486_143220_1913142"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that heightens the color contrast of some text and images on your screen, making those items more distinct and easier to identify.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="143220">High Contrast</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913142">අධි ප්‍රභේදනය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24868_1162904_1913516"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The portion of data distribution that is determined to be more or less than some critical value. For example, the far left and far right areas of a bell curve.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1162904">tail</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913516">වාලය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24869_1162906_1913517"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A test in which the null hypothesis is rejected if the value of the test statistic falls into either tail of the probability distribution (i.e. is either less than a first critical value or greater than a second critical value).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1162906">two-tailed test</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913517">ද්වි-වල්ගා පිරික්සුම</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24869_1162906_1913531"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A test in which the null hypothesis is rejected if the value of the test statistic falls into either tail of the probability distribution (i.e. is either less than a first critical value or greater than a second critical value).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1162906">two-tailed test</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913531">ද්වි-පාර්ශවික පිරික්සුම</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24869_1176836_1913517"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A test in which the null hypothesis is rejected if the value of the test statistic falls into either tail of the probability distribution (i.e. is either less than a first critical value or greater than a second critical value).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1176836">two-sided test</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913517">ද්වි-වල්ගා පිරික්සුම</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24869_1176836_1913531"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A test in which the null hypothesis is rejected if the value of the test statistic falls into either tail of the probability distribution (i.e. is either less than a first critical value or greater than a second critical value).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1176836">two-sided test</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913531">ද්වි-පාර්ශවික පිරික්සුම</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech