Resource Interchange File Format (RIFF) specification.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="136267">AVI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635742">ශ්‍රව්‍ය දෘශ්‍ය අතුරුමාරුව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5114_139328_634322"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Web Storage System content class defines the intent or purpose of an item along with the names of properties that are intended for items in this class.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="139328">content class</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634322">අන්තර්ගත පන්තිය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5117_262544_1368682"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual effect that imparts a quality of translucency to windows.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262544">glass</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1368682">කවුළු වීදුරුව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5117_262544_635716"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual effect that imparts a quality of translucency to windows.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262544">glass</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635716">වීදුරුව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5117_777772_1368682"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual effect that imparts a quality of translucency to windows.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="777772">window glass</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1368682">කවුළු වීදුරුව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5117_777772_635716"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual effect that imparts a quality of translucency to windows.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="777772">window glass</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635716">වීදුරුව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5119_319158_634857"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The distance or period of time between a specified start point and a specified end point. For example, the length of an audio or video clip is usually measured in minutes and seconds.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="319158">length</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634857">දිග</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="512_14369_1801121"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of chart that displays the trend of values over time or categories. By displaying the sum of the plotted values, an area chart also shows the relationship of parts to a whole.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="14369">area chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1801121">ප්‍රස්ථාර ප්‍රදේශ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5121_73528_1913067"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of symbolic resolution where a symbol is resolved to a specific software routine during program execution instead of during program compilation, enabling polymorphism in object-oriented programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="73528">late binding</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913067">පසු බැඳුම්</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5121_73529_1913067"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of symbolic resolution where a symbol is resolved to a specific software routine during program execution instead of during program compilation, enabling polymorphism in object-oriented programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="73529">dynamic binding</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913067">පසු බැඳුම්</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5123_26059_636039"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To store frequently used data values in a special memory subsystem for quick access.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="26059">cache</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="636039">හැඹිලිගත කරන්න</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5127_340084_634455"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To add new text, objects or cells without overwriting existing data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="340084">insert</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634455">ඇතුළු කරන්න</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5128_319431_634470"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to characters that are evenly slanted to the right or in the direction of text flow.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="319431">italic</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634470">ඇලකුරු</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5129_415567_635953"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An action or occurrence to which a program might respond. Examples include state changes, data transfers, key presses, and mouse movements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="415567">program event</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635953">සිද්ධිය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5129_51961_635953"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An action or occurrence to which a program might respond. Examples include state changes, data transfers, key presses, and mouse movements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="51961">event</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635953">සිද්ධිය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5131_159863_635093"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of detecting and splitting video content into separate clips. Clips are created by Windows Movie Maker when there is a significant change from one frame to another.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="159863">clip creation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635093">පසුරූ නිර්මාණකරණය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5151_228751_635787"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A real-time communication session between two or more users, which can involve IM, video, or audio.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="228751">conversation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635787">සංවාදය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5158_154233_634146"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An industry-standard Internet tunneling protocol that provides encapsulation for sending Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) frames across packet-oriented media. For IP networks, L2TP traffic is sent as User Datagram Protocol (UDP) messages. In Microsoft operating systems, L2TP is used in conjunction with Internet Protocol security (IPSec) as a virtual private network (VPN) technology to provide remote access or router-to-router VPN connections. L2TP is described in RFC 2661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="154233">Layer Two Tunneling Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634146">L2TP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5158_154233_634880"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An industry-standard Internet tunneling protocol that provides encapsulation for sending Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) frames across packet-oriented media. For IP networks, L2TP traffic is sent as User Datagram Protocol (UDP) messages. In Microsoft operating systems, L2TP is used in conjunction with Internet Protocol security (IPSec) as a virtual private network 