age communicate with another program written in an unknown language. An IDL is used to define interfaces between client and server programs. For example, an IDL can provide interfaces to remote CORBA objects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="731998">IDL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1801153">IDL</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7002_157648_634658"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A time limit that is applied to the life of an account, so that it can be used only for a predetermined period of time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="157648">account expiration</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634658">ගිණුම් කල් ඉකුත්වීම</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7010_1249014_1370242"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An auxiliary software component that extends or enhances the features of other software.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1249014">callout</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1370242">ප්ලගිනය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="part