ter or device uses to perform a specific task, such as word processing, accounting, or data management.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="95381">application</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1520631">යෙදු</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7702_95381_634561"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of instructions that a computer or device uses to perform a specific task, such as word processing, accounting, or data management.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="95381">application</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634561">ක්‍රමලේඛය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7702_95381_635432"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of instructions that a computer or device uses to perform a specific task, such as word processing, accounting, or data management.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="95381">application</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635432">යෙදුම</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7703_145418_1913163"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The file on your hard disk that contains offline folders. The offline folder file has an .ost extension. You can create it automatically when you set up Outlook, or when you first make a folder available offline.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="145418">offline folder file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913163">නොබැඳි ෆෝල්ඩර ගොනුව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7712_130661_1370253"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An area of storage on a hard disk. A volume is formatted by using a file system, such as NTFS, and has a drive letter assigned to it. A single hard disk can have multiple volumes. Some volumes can span multiple hard disks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="130661">volume</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1370253">වෙළුම</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7719_175788_1368718"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A handle (often, a tall, thin rectangle) that appears on a rebar or command band. By touching and dragging a gripper bar with a stylus or mouse, a user can reposition or resize a rebar or command band.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="175788">gripper bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1368718">ග්‍රාහකය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7719_770797_1368718"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A handle (often, a tall, thin rectangle) that appears on a rebar or command band. By touching and dragging a gripper bar with a stylus or mouse, a user can reposition or resize a rebar or command band.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="770797">gripper</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1368718">ග්‍රාහකය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7735_1136138_634622"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of UI controls that appear in context when an object is selected and contain actions that act upon the object.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1136138">mini-toolbar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634622">කුඩා මෙවලම් තීරුව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7735_317879_634622"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of UI controls that appear in context when an object is selected and contain actions that act upon the object.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="317879">Mini toolbar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634622">කුඩා මෙවලම් තීරුව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7738_50933_2178125"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tag that closes an element: &lt;/&gt;. An end tag follows the syntax &lt;/Name&gt;, where Name matches the element name declared in the start tag.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="50933">end tag</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2178125">අන්ත ඇමුණුම</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7749_294442_635466"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of related fields (columns) of information treated as a unit and arranged in a horizontal line in a table or spreadsheet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="294442">row</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635466">රෙකෝඩය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7749_294442_636747"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of related fields (columns) of information treated as a unit and arranged in a horizontal line in a table or spreadsheet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="294442">row</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="636747">පේළිය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7749_99659_635466"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of related fields (columns) of information treated as a unit and arranged in a horizontal line in a table or spreadsheet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="99659">record</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635466">රෙකෝඩය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7749_99659_636747"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of related fields (columns) of information treated as a unit and arranged in a horizontal line in a table or spreadsheet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="99659">record</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="636747">පේළිය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7753_42713_1913050"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A bar, area, dot, slice, or other symbol in a chart that represents a single data point or value.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="42713">data marker</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1913050">දත්ත සලකුණුකරණය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="776_149884_635721"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of comments that users attach to web pages and documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="149884">Web discussion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635721">වෙබ් කතිකාව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7764_1975517_1981852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hard disk that contains a small amount of solid-state nonvolatile memory which, when used as a cache, can realize significant benefits such as faster booting, extended battery life, and a more rugged PC.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1975517">hybrid drive</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981852">උසස් ධාවකය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7764_314130_1981852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hard disk that contains a small amount of solid-state nonvolatile memory which, when used as a cache, can realize significant benefits such as faster booting, extended battery life, and a more rugged PC.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="314130">hybrid hard disk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981852">උසස් ධාවකය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7764_366903_1981852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hard disk that contains a small amount of solid-state nonvolatile memory which, when used as a cache, can realize significant benefits such as faster booting, extended battery life, and a more rugged PC.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="366903">hybrid disk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1981852">උසස් ධාවකය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7781_179526_635265"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A control (composed of a text box and spin button control) that allows a user to adjust a value from a limited range of possible values.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="179526">spin box</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="635265">බැමුම් මංජුසාව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7785_120062_634600"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The bar that contains the 'Start' button and appears by default at the bottom of the desktop. You can click the taskbar buttons to switch between programs. You can also hide the taskbar, move it to the sides or top of the desktop, and customize it in other ways.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120062">taskbar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634600">කාර්ය තීරුව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7785_2785563_634600"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The bar that contains the 'Start' button and appears by default at the bottom of the desktop. You can click the taskbar buttons to switch between programs. You can also hide the taskbar, move it to the sides or top of the desktop, and customize it in other ways.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2785563">task bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634600">කාර්ය තීරුව</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7797_54308_634677"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In an operating system, the overall structure in which files are named, stored, and organized. NTFS, FAT, and FAT32 are types of file systems.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="54308">file system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="si-LK"><ntig><termGrp><term id="634677">ගොනු පද්ධතිය</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LKA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="78_1803_635361"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A webpage that serves as the starting point of a website.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1803">home page</